{"body":{"began":"2026-11-11T20:07:47.993Z","purpose":"What the last cycle left: a commit to a store no longer has its index built whole, nor its blocks read again. The index is patched by the holons whose version or whose types changed, and gives exactly what a fresh one gives, in the same order, which a test holds it to; a store opened again keeps the blocks already read, as they are named by their hash. Measured before and after: main, 116 thousand holons, 690 thousand facts, about 470 ms to index and 500 to read again.","said":[],"stands":"running","step":"A changed store's index patched"},"id":"1M763JHGS7YR000","instance":["1M75J5K9VFY6000"],"name":"A changed store's index patched","prev":null}
